# https://w3id.org/sso#ydir
<https://w3id.org/sso#ydir> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ydir> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ydir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/sso#SurfaceLoad> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ydir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ydir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Y component of a Surface Load's direction vector."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ydir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Y direction component"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#yield_stress
<https://w3id.org/sso#yield_stress> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#yield_stress> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#yield_stress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/sso#PlasticBehaviour> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#yield_stress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#yield_stress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The stress at which the material begins to deform plastically."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#yield_stress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "yield stress"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#zdir
<https://w3id.org/sso#zdir> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#zdir> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#zdir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/sso#SurfaceLoad> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#zdir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#zdir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Z component of a Surface Load's direction vector."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#zdir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Z direction component"@en .
# 
# 
# 
# #################################################################
# #
# #    Classes
# #
# #################################################################
# 
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#ArbitraryProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#ArbitraryProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ArbitraryProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ArbitraryProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An arbitrary polygonal cross-section, optionally with holes; its point geometry isn't structurally modeled in this ontology."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ArbitraryProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Arbitrary Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Assembly
<https://w3id.org/sso#Assembly> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Assembly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The collection of Instances that, together, position the model's Objects in the global coordinate system — the assembled structural model on which Sets, Loads, and Boundary Conditions are defined."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Assembly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assembly"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#BeamElement
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamElement> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#Element> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A finite element idealizing a slender linear structural member, such as a beam or column, via its cross-section."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamElement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Beam Element"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#BeamSection
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamSection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#Section> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A section assigning a named beam profile and orientation to beam elements, carrying exactly one typed Cross-Section Profile for its geometry."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BeamSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Beam Section"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#BoundaryCondition
<https://w3id.org/sso#BoundaryCondition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BoundaryCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A restraint or prescribed displacement applied to a node set, specified per degree of freedom (ux, uy, uz, rx, ry, rz)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BoundaryCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Boundary Condition"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#BoxProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#BoxProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BoxProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BoxProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A rectangular hollow cross-section, defined by its outer width/height and wall thicknesses."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#BoxProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Box Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Calibration
<https://w3id.org/sso#Calibration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Calibration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Calibration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A provenance-bearing event (a prov:Activity) that produces a calibrated snapshot of a model parameter from a baseline, using measured test data."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Calibration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Calibration"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#CircProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#CircProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#CircProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#CircProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A solid circular cross-section, defined by its radius."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#CircProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Circular Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#CoordinateSystem
<https://w3id.org/sso#CoordinateSystem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#CoordinateSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A local coordinate system defined by its X, Y, and Z axis vectors."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#CoordinateSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Coordinate System"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The parametric geometric shape of a beam's cross-section — an abstract type with concrete parametric profiles such as Rectangular, Box, and I-Profile — assigned to a Beam Section."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cross-Section Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#DistributedLoad
<https://w3id.org/sso#DistributedLoad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#DistributedLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#Load> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#DistributedLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A load distributed linearly along an element edge/line, defined by its direction and end values."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#DistributedLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Distributed Load"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#ElasticBehaviour
<https://w3id.org/sso#ElasticBehaviour> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ElasticBehaviour> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The linear-elastic constitutive response of a material, defined by its behaviour type (isotropic, anisotropic, or orthotropic) and elastic parameters (Young's modulus, Poisson's ratio)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#ElasticBehaviour> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Elastic Behaviour"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Element
<https://w3id.org/sso#Element> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Element> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A discretized finite element in a structural mesh, the basic unit solved by the analysis (e.g. a solid, shell, or beam element)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Element> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Finite Element"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Elset
<https://w3id.org/sso#Elset> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Elset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named group of elements, defined on an assembled Instance, used to scope distributed and surface loads to a specific part of the model."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Elset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Element Set"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#GeneralProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#GeneralProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#GeneralProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#GeneralProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A cross-section defined directly by its section properties (area, moments of inertia, torsional constant) rather than by shape."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#GeneralProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "General Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#HexProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#HexProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#HexProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#HexProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A hexagonal hollow cross-section, defined by its circumscribed radius and wall thickness."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#HexProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hexagonal Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#IProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#IProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#IProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#IProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An I-shaped (wide-flange) cross-section, defined by its overall depth, flange widths and thicknesses, and web thickness."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#IProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "I-Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Instance
<https://w3id.org/sso#Instance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A placement of a structural Object within the Assembly: references the Object and applies the spatial transformation between the Object's local coordinate system and the model's global coordinate system. Multiple Instances may reference the same Object to replicate an identical mesh without duplicating its data, and carry their own Node/Element Sets for scoping loads and boundary conditions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Instance"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#LProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#LProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#LProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#LProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An L-shaped (angle) cross-section, defined by its two leg widths and thicknesses."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#LProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "L-Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Load
<https://w3id.org/sso#Load> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Load> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An action applied to the structure within a Load Case — a point, distributed, or surface load."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Load> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Load"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#LoadCase
<https://w3id.org/sso#LoadCase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#LoadCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named grouping of loads applied together in one analysis case, optionally including a self-weight contribution."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#LoadCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Load Case"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Material
<https://w3id.org/sso#Material> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Material> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A structural material, assigned to elements via a Section, whose constitutive behaviour is decomposed into a required Elastic Behaviour and an optional Plastic Behaviour, alongside its density."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Material> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Material"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Mesh
<https://w3id.org/sso#Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The finite element discretization of an Object: its nodes and elements."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Mesh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mesh"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Node
<https://w3id.org/sso#Node> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A meshed point in space, identified by its coordinates, that finite elements connect to."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Node"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Nset
<https://w3id.org/sso#Nset> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Nset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A named group of nodes, defined on an assembled Instance, used to scope loads and boundary conditions to a specific part of the model."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Nset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Node Set"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Object
<https://w3id.org/sso#Object> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A structural component (e.g. a beam, shell, or solid assembly) defined in its own local coordinate system: its Mesh of Nodes and Elements, referencing Sections and Materials. An Object is defined once and positioned in the model via one or more Instances."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Structural Object"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#PipeProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#PipeProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PipeProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PipeProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A circular hollow cross-section, defined by its outer radius and wall thickness."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PipeProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pipe Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#PlasticBehaviour
<https://w3id.org/sso#PlasticBehaviour> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PlasticBehaviour> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The plastic (post-yield) constitutive response of a material, defined by its yield stress and plastic strain."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PlasticBehaviour> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Plastic Behaviour"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#PointLoad
<https://w3id.org/sso#PointLoad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PointLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#Load> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PointLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A concentrated load applied to a single degree of freedom of a node set."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#PointLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Point Load"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#RectProfile
<https://w3id.org/sso#RectProfile> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#RectProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/sso#CrossSectionProfile> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#RectProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A solid rectangular cross-section, defined by its width and height."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#RectProfile> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rectangular Profile"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#Section
<https://w3id.org/sso#Section> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Section> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A structural section that assigns geometric and material properties to the elements referencing it; an abstract type with three concrete kinds — Beam, Shell, and Solid Section."@en .
<https://w3id.org/sso#Section> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Section"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/sso#ShellElement
